   "label": "f04-schedule-race",
   "front": "How can one scheduled tick produce two runs?",
   "back": "The scheduler loop and the internal dispatch route can run dispatchScheduledRuns concurrently; it reads due workflows, enqueues, then advances nextScheduledAt with no lock. Fix: claim with a conditional update on nextScheduledAt and enqueue only if one row changed.",
   "observation": "read-derived",
