   "shape": "hand-authored",
   "label": "f01-execute-route",
   "front": "In what order does executeRoute handle a request, and how are errors mapped?",
   "back": "Load the session actor; if the route needs a permission, 401 without an actor, then assertPermission (403); then parse the body; then run the handler. AppError keeps its status; anything else (ZodError, SyntaxError, Prisma errors) becomes a generic 500 and is not logged.",
   "observation": "read-derived",
